MySQL Connector/J
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The jffast distribution bundles MySQL Connector/J (com.mysql:mysql-connector-j),
which is licensed under:

  The GNU General Public License, v2 with Universal FOSS Exception, v1.0
  (https://www.mysql.com/about/legal/connector-j/)

The Universal FOSS Exception is what makes this combination distributable:
it grants permission to use, link, and redistribute Connector/J as part of a
work whose own license is not GPL, while the GPL text continues to govern
Connector/J itself. Without the exception, redistributing a GPL component inside
an Apache-2.0-licensed binary would not be permitted.

The driver is included so that the released fat jar runs against MySQL out of
the box. Applications targeting another database do not need it.

The other JDBC drivers are declared "optional" in jffast-starter-mybatis, so
they are never pulled in transitively and are explicitly excluded from the
distribution artifact. They must be supplied by the deploying party, by
adding the one matching the target database to the application's own build:

  - PostgreSQL JDBC (org.postgresql:postgresql) - BSD 2-Clause
  - Oracle JDBC (com.oracle.database.jdbc:ojdbc11) - Oracle Free Use Terms
    and Conditions (FUTC) -- NOT an OSI-approved license
  - DM (com.dameng:DmJdbcDriver18) and Kingbase (cn.com.kingbase:kingbase8) -
    vendor-specific proprietary terms -- NOT OSI-approved licenses

Only the non-MySQL drivers whose licenses are not OSI-approved are excluded
for legal reasons; PostgreSQL's driver is excluded for consistency with the
single-driver default, not because of its license.
